# Kept in the repository, left out of what a release distributes: `git
# archive`, the source tarballs GitHub builds from a tag, and the Akku
# archive, which serves exactly `git archive` of the tag. `akku install`
# unpacks the whole package into each consumer's .akku/src/chez-libuv/, so
# whatever the archive holds reaches every consumer. These paths are for
# working on the repository, not for using it: design records, plans and
# the early experiments, instructions for coding agents, the contributor
# guide, and CI. `make check-archive` fails if any of them would ship, or
# if anything else would not.
/.plans export-ignore
/spike export-ignore
/AGENTS.md export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
/.github export-ignore
